[00:37.98]Hello Reason, my old friend
[00:41.02]It seems we have abandoned you again
[00:44.86]Like with a sickness slowly creeping
[00:47.76]Left our sacred duty sleeping
[00:51.08]And the chicken sacrificed for all your sins
[00:56.52]Where no one wins
[00:59.82]Begins the sound of violence
[01:05.86]Sometimes it seems we walk alone
[01:14.44]We search for Reason then we know
[01:17.64]There is no hero coming to save me
[01:21.06]If men are weak and women are crazy
[01:24.46]Heroes are forged in the fires of the choices they've made
[01:29.68]That no one makes
[01:33.14]We hear the sound of violence
[01:40.16]
[01:45.34]And in the dusk of our brightest day
[01:48.70]The future darkens as they invade
[01:52.06]Consuming without producing
[01:54.84]Breeding only debt and tyranny
[01:58.22]Trading our time for their obligations
[02:02.30]And no one cares
[02:08.00]So grows the sound of violence
[02:13.42]
[02:52.16]Fools are we, do we not know
[02:55.18]The root from which this violence grows?
[02:59.08]Take your accounting seriously
[03:01.60]Do not shun responsibility
[03:04.42]Before the swine, these cast pearls fell
[03:10.40]We sense the swell
[03:15.62]The rising swell of violence
[03:20.46]And the people cowered as they prayed
[03:24.34]But our heroes had all turned gay
[03:27.78]Then JustSomeGuy™ spoke out his warning:
[03:31.26]Legal is the law of surety and accounting
[03:35.72]Write your own ledger or prepare for harm from strangers
[03:43.48]JustSomeGuy™ tried to quell the violence
[03:47.24]
